<p><font SIZE=+3>Fife Lake (2784)</font></p>

<p><font size=+1><a href="smry.pdf">All
tables for this station in Adobe Acrobat format</a></font>

<p>&nbsp;The following tables are the 1951-1980 Normals and Narrative Summary</p>

<p>1. <a HREF="tmp1_nm.txt">Temperature normals and extremes</a></p>

<p>2. <a HREF="tmp2_nm.txt">Heating &amp; cooling degree days, and number of
days for selected thresholds </a></p>

<p>3. <a HREF="prec_nm.txt">Precipitation normals </a></p>

<p>4. <a HREF="narrat.txt">Narrative summary</a> </p>

<p>The following tables are statistical probabilities based on the 1951-1980
data</p>

<p>using the indicated Probability Distribution Function (PDF). </p>

<p>5. <a HREF="tmax_st.txt">Average daily maximum temperature (Normal PDF)</a></p>

<p>6. <a HREF="tmin_st.txt">Average daily minimum temperature (Normal PDF)
</a></p>

<p>7. <a HREF="tmen_st.txt">Average daily mean temperature (Normal PDF)</a></p>

<p>8. <a HREF="hdd65_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (July-June) heating degree-days
base 65 F (Gamma PDF)</a> </p>

<p>9. <a HREF="cdd65_st.txt">Monthly &amp; annual cooling degree days-base
65 F (Gamma PDF) </a></p>

<p>10. <a HREF="txg90_st.txt">Number of days with maximum Temperature of 90
F or above (Weibull PDF)</a></p>

<p>11. <a HREF="txl32_st.txt">Number of days with maximum Temperature of 32
F or below (Weibull PDF)</a></p>

<p>12. <a HREF="tnl32_st.txt">Number of days with minimum Temperature of 32
F or below (Weibull PDF) </a></p>

<p>13. <a HREF="tnl0_st.txt">Number of days with minimum Temperature of 0 F
or below (Weibull PDF) </a></p>

<p>14. <a HREF="l_spr_st.txt">Last spring temperature threshold date (Normal
PDF)</a> </p>

<p>15. <a HREF="f_fal_st.txt">First fall temperature threshold date (Normal
PDF)</a> </p>

<p>16. <a HREF="g_sea_st.txt">Growing season length between threshold dates
(Normal PDF)</a> </p>

<p>17. <a HREF="gdd40_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days
base 40 F (Gamma PDF)</a></p>

<p>18. <a HREF="gdd45_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days
base 45 F (Gamma PDF)</a></p>

<p>19. <a HREF="gdd50_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days
base 50 F (Gamma PDF)</a></p>

<p>20. <a HREF="gdd55_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days
base 55 F (Gamma PDF)</a></p>

<p>21. <a HREF="g8650_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Mar-Oct) growing degree-days,
corn method (86max &amp; 50min) (Gamma PDF) </a></p>

<p>22. <a HREF="prec_st.txt">Monthly &amp; annual total precipitation (Gamma
PDF) </a></p>

<p>23. <a HREF="snow_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Sep-May) total snowfall
(Gamma PDF) </a></p>

<p>24. <a HREF="dpg10_st.txt"># of days with precipitation of .10 inch or above
(Weibull PDF)</a> </p>

<p>25. <a HREF="dpg25_st.txt"># of days with precipitation of .25 inch or above
(Weibull PDF) </a></p>

<p>26. <a HREF="dpg50_st.txt"># of days with precipitation of .50 inch or above
(Weibull PDF) </a></p>

<p>27. <a HREF="prssn_st.txt">Monthly &amp; seasonal (Apr-Sep) precipitation
(Gamma PDF) </a></p>

<p>28. Grouping of all Normals tables (Archived) </p>

<p>29. Grouping of all temperature related files (Archived) </p>

